-- title:
--   The vertex chart as a localisation of the edge chart mod πⁿ⁺¹
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring, $\pi \in \mathcal O$, let $r$ be a prime and $n$ a natural number. Write $A =$ `chartERing 𝒪 π r`, the localisation of $\bigl(\mathcal O[X_0,X_1]/(\mathtt{edgeRel}\,\mathcal O\,\pi)\bigr)$ away from the class of $\mathtt{edgeDiscr}\,\mathcal O\,r$, and $V =$ `chartVRing 𝒪 r`, the localisation of $\mathcal O[X]$ away from $X^r - X$; both carry distinguished elements, $\xi, \eta \in A$ and $\zeta \in V$. The assertion is that there exists an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism
--   $$\iota : A/(\pi^{n+1}) \longrightarrow V/(\pi^{n+1}),$$
--   where in each case the ideal is the one generated by the image of $\pi^{n+1}$ under the structure map, such that: $\iota$ carries the class of $\xi$ to the class of $\zeta$; the product of $\iota(\eta \bmod \pi^{n+1})$ with the class of $\zeta$ equals the image of $\pi$ in $V/(\pi^{n+1})$; and, with $V/(\pi^{n+1})$ regarded as an $A/(\pi^{n+1})$-algebra via $\iota$, it is a localisation of $A/(\pi^{n+1})$ away from the class of $\xi$, i.e. `IsLocalization.Away` holds for that element. Thus, informally, $\iota(\eta) = \pi\zeta^{-1}$ and $V/(\pi^{n+1}) \cong (A/(\pi^{n+1}))[\xi^{-1}]$.
--
--   This is the compatibility, at each level $n$, between the vertex charts and the edge charts of the standard formal model of the $p$-adic upper half plane: modulo $\pi^{n+1}$ the vertex chart ring is obtained from the edge chart ring by inverting the coordinate $\xi$. It is used in the construction of the Mumford gluing data, being cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.nonempty_mumfordGlueLevel_of_isSchottky`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.nonempty_mumfordGlueLevel_of_isSchottky).
